                     /gene="ycf65"
                     /locus_tag="GFC16_pgp137"
                     /note="Probable plastid-specific 30S ribosomal protein 3
                     (PSRP-3)or Ycf65-like protein. This small acidic protein
                     is found in 30S ribosomal subunit of cyanobacteria and
                     plant plastids. In plants it has been named plastid-
                     specific ribosomal protein 3 (PSRP-3), and in
                     cyanobacteria it is named Ycf65. Plastid-specific
                     ribosomal proteins may mediate the effects of nuclear
                     factors on plastid translation. The acidic PSRPs are
                     thought to contribute to protein-protein interactions in
                     the 30S subunit, and are not thought to bind RNA."
                     /codon_start=1
                     /transl_table=11
