                     /gene="rps10"
                     /locus_tag="GFC16_pgp114"
                     /note="Ribosomal protein S10 is one of the proteins from
                     30S large ribosomal subunit. S10 consists of about 100
                     amino acid residues. In Escherichia coli, S10 is involved
                     in binding tRNA to the ribosome, and also operates as a
                     transcriptional elongation factor. Experimental evidence
                     has revealed that S10 has virtually no groups exposed on
                     the ribosomal surface."
                     /codon_start=1
                     /transl_table=11
                     /product="30S ribosomal protein S10"
