                     /locus_tag="GFC16_pgp100"
                     /note="Ribosomal protein L6 is one of the proteins from
                     50S large ribosomal subunit. In Escherichia coli, it is
                     located in the aminoacyl-tRNA binding site of the
                     peptidyltransferase centre, and is known to bind directly
                     to 23S rRNA. L6 comprises 2 almost identical folds,
                     suggesting that is was derived by the duplication of an
                     ancient RNA-binding protein gene. Analysis reveals several
                     sites on the protein surface where interactions with other
                     ribosome components may occur, the N-terminus being
                     involved in protein-protein interactions and the C-
                     terminus containing possible RNA-binding sites."
                     /codon_start=1
                     /transl_table=11
                     /product="50S ribosomal protein L6"
