                     /locus_tag="GFC16_pgp081"
                     /note="Members of this protein family represent one of two
                     essential proteins of system II for c-type cytochrome
                     biogenesis. This protein is designated CcsB in some
                     bacteria, resC in Bacillus, and CcsA in chloroplasts.
                     CcsA, proposed to be a heme delivery factor, is speculated
                     to interact physically in vivo with Ccs1, an apoprotein
                     chaperone, and these proteins are involved in the
                     catalyzed process, leading to the conversion of
                     apocytochromes f and c(6) to their respective holoforms."
                     /codon_start=1
