                     /note="Cytochrome C550 (CytC550) is a class 1A cytochrome.
                     CytC550 (also known as PsbV) is an extrinsic membrane
                     protein that forms part of the oxygen-evolving complex in
                     photosystem II, this complex being responsible for the
                     splitting of water into O(2) and 4H+, the latter being
                     used to reduce CO2 to glucose. CytC550 is only found in
                     cyanobacteria and red algae, this protein having been lost
                     during the evolution of green plants."
