                     /note="The cytochrome b6 is an integral membrane protein,
                     and a component of the plastoquinone-plastocyanin
                     reductase, also known as the cytochrome b6f complex. It
                     belongs to the cytochrome b/b6 family. In plants and
                     cyanobacteria, cytochrome b6 is analogous to eukaryote
                     cytochrome b, containing two chains: helices A-D are
                     encoded by the petB gene and helices E-H are encoded by
                     the petD gene in these organisms."
