                     /note="This family consists of the photosystem I reaction
                     centre subunit IX. PsaJ protein is a small 4.4kDa,
                     chloroplast encoded, hydrophobic subunit of the PSI
                     reaction complex whose function is not yet fully
                     understood. PsaJ has a proposed role in maintaining PsaF
                     in the correct orientation to allow for fast electron
                     transfer from soluble donor proteins to P700."
