                     /locus_tag="GFC16_pgp026"
                     /note="A functional Tat system or Delta pH-dependent
                     pathway requires three integral membrane proteins:
                     TatA/Tha4, TatB/Hcf106 and TatC/cpTatC. The TatC protein
                     (also named ycf43) is essential for the function of both
                     pathways. It might be involved in twin-arginine signal
                     peptide recognition, protein translocation and proton
                     translocation."
