                     /locus_tag="GFC16_pgp023"
                     /note="The Ycf3 protein is loosely associated with the
                     thylakoid membrane. This suggests that Ycf3 is not part of
                     a stable complex and that it probably interacts
                     transiently with its partners, BtpA (IPR005137) and Ycf4.
                     Ycf3 contains a number of tetratrico peptide repeats
                     (TPR), which are structural motifs present in a wide range
                     of proteins and mediate proteinprotein interactions."
