                     /note="Ribosomal protein S18 is one of the proteins from
                     the 30S small ribosomal subunit. S18 is known to be
                     involved in binding the aminoacyl-tRNA complex in
                     Escherichia coli, and appears to be situated at the tRNA
                     A- site. Experimental evidence has revealed that S18 is
                     well exposed on the surface of the E. coli ribosome, and
                     is a secondary rRNA binding protein."
