                     /EC_number="1.18.-.-"
                     /note="Ferredoxin thioredoxin reductase is a [4FE-4S]
                     protein which plays an important role in the
                     ferredoxin/thioredoxin regulatory chain. It converts an
                     electron signal (photoreduced ferredoxin) to a thiol
                     signal (reduced thioredoxin), regulating enzymes by
                     reduction of specific disulphide groups. It catalyses the
                     light-dependent activation of several photosynthetis
                     enzymes. Ferredoxin thioredoxin reductase is a heterodimer
                     of subunit a and subunit b. Subunit a is the variable
                     subunit, and b is the catalytic chain. This family is the
                     beta chain."
                     /codon_start=1
                     /transl_table=11
